\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Evaluation scenario: (a) Referring to the Fig. \ref {fig:rke-cls}, the load generator is located on Machine A to simulate the user experience latency in accessing the overall systems. While the System Under Test (SUT) is the target to be evaluated and is located on Machine B. The connectivity used to trunk the request from Machine A ({\it  wrk2}, which fires the HTTP/1.1 request) to Machine B is utilizing a 25 Gbps Ethernet network. Frontend, at this phase, will accept all incoming HTTP requests and translate them into gRPC requests using the proxy gateway interface defined in its deployment configuration. (b) Isolated evaluation of the backend service that runs partially inside the SUT cluster. This evaluation is performed using {\it  ghz} performance tool, which aims to eliminate the queuing effect caused by the communication mesh at the frontend service and to measure the pure computational backend service time.}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
